@startuml seq-create-booking
!theme plain
title Sign in and create a booking

actor Student
participant "labbook-web\n(SPA + nginx)" as Web
participant "ThunderID" as IDP
participant "labbook-api" as API
database PostgreSQL as DB

Student -> Web : open app, click Sign in
Web -> IDP : redirect to /oauth2/authorize (code + PKCE challenge)
Student -> IDP : sign in (password entered at ThunderID)
IDP --> Web : redirect to /auth/callback?code=...
Web -> IDP : POST /idp/token via nginx (code + PKCE verifier)
IDP --> Web : access token (JWT)
Student -> Web : submit booking form
Web -> API : POST /api/bookings + Authorization: Bearer <jwt>
API -> API : verify JWT signature (JWKS) and issuer, resolve caller + role
API -> DB : load resource, count upcoming bookings
API -> API : check rules BR-1..BR-5, BR-7, BR-8
alt a rule is broken
  API --> Web : 422 {code: RULE_VIOLATION, rule: BR-n}
else rules pass
  API -> DB : INSERT booking
  alt exclusion constraint (SQLSTATE 23P01)
    DB --> API : conflicting key value
    API --> Web : 409 {code: BOOKING_CONFLICT}
  else free slot
    DB --> API : row
    API --> Web : 201 booking (pending, or approved for admins)
  end
end
Web --> Student : show result or inline error
@enduml
